# ==========================
# OS / Base Image Issues
# ==========================

# ncurses fix blocked by glibc upgrade requirement, waiting for backport or fix in next Debian stable release.
CVE-2025-6141
CVE-2025-69720

# zlib - CPU consumption/DoS vulnerability. Fixed in zlib 1.3.2. Waiting for backport or fix in next Debian stable release.
CVE-2026-27171

# Hidden File Injection in tar — mitigate by not extracting untrusted tar files.
CVE-2026-5704

# Privilege escalation and symlink traversal / out-of-bounds write in tar. Waiting for fix to be released by tar maintainers.
CVE-2026-18477
CVE-2026-18508

# Hostname spoofing in util-linux. Waiting for fix in unstable - fix might only be possible in next Debian stable release.
CVE-2026-3184

# Out-of-bounds write in libc. Waiting for fix in unstable - risks with backporting / upgrading glibc - fix might only be possible in next Debian stable release.
CVE-2026-5435

# DNS Verification Bypass in libc. Waiting for fix in unstable - risks with backporting / upgrading glibc - fix might only be possible in next Debian stable release.
CVE-2026-6238

# perl vulnerabilities - waiting for fixes to be released by perl maintainers or in Debian stable.
CVE-2026-9538

# Symlink traversal in acl. Fix released by acl maintainers - waiting for fix to be released in Debian stable.
CVE-2026-54370
CVE-2026-54369

# Symlink traversal in attr. Fix released by attr maintainers - waiting for fix to be released in Debian stable.
CVE-2026-54371

# Denial of Service in bzip2. Waiting for fix to be released in Debian stable.
CVE-2026-42250

# Timing discrepancy / Plaintext password recovery in linux-pam. Only exploitable when pam_userdb is configured with crypt=none.
CVE-2026-54411

# Null pointer reference / Denial of Service, and Information disclosure in libsqlite3. Fixed in sqlite3 3.53.2-1 - waiting for fix to be released in Debian stable.
CVE-2026-50812
CVE-2026-50813

# GPG Validation in apt. Waiting for fix to be released in Debian stable.
CVE-2011-3374

# Path traversal / arbitrary process termination in systemd-oomd, and local privilege escalation in systemd-homed (libudev1). Not exploitable in this image - systemd-oomd/systemd-homed are not present/running in this container. Fix only available in forky/sid.
CVE-2026-15059
CVE-2026-16742

# Arbitrary code execution / OOB memory access, and incorrect regex matching in perl regex engine (perl-base). Not reachable via any code path in this image (Perl not invoked as a service). Waiting for fix to be released in Debian stable.
CVE-2026-15534
CVE-2026-19487

# Heap buffer overflow via fopen ccs=, buffer overflow in strfmon, out-of-bounds write in tdelete, process abort/DoS and stack exhaustion in wordexp, and infinite loop/hang in iconv SHIFT_JISX0213/EUC_JISX0213 conversion (libc). None of these code paths are used by the Python stdlib or in this image. Waiting for fix to be released in Debian stable.
CVE-2026-18374
CVE-2026-19499
CVE-2026-19542
CVE-2026-6368
CVE-2026-6791
CVE-2026-77117
CVE-2026-80489

# Privilege escalation via unchecked mount post-hooks, nsenter --join-cgroup cgroup migration authority leak, X-mount.subdir symlink traversal, and bind mount source redirection in util-linux. Not applicable to this image - no fstab-based mount workflow or nsenter usage; runs as non-root entrypoint. Waiting for fix to be released in Debian stable.
CVE-2026-76642
CVE-2026-78408
CVE-2026-78409
CVE-2026-78410

# Stack overflow / DoS in nscd via oversized DNS response (libc). Not exploitable in this image - nscd is not installed/running. No fix currently available upstream.
CVE-2026-89092

# Heap buffer overflow in zlib (1.3.1.2-1.3.2). No upstream fix released yet (Debian bug #1146895). zlib is used broadly for compression/decompression (including via Python's zlib module) - flagged for re-assessment once an upstream/Debian fix lands.
CVE-2026-85091

# Denial of Service (assertion failure/process abort) in glibc DNS stub resolver via long search domain in resolv.conf. Requires an attacker-influenced /etc/resolv.conf (e.g. malicious DHCP/VPN) - flagged for re-assessment given any Python code performing DNS resolution relies on this resolver. Fixed in glibc 2.43-6 (sid) - waiting for fix to be released in Debian stable.
CVE-2026-8674

# Memory exhaustion in perl. Not exploitable; documented in POLICY_CONFIGURATION.md.
CVE-2026-82560

# ==========================
# Python Issues
# ==========================

# Fixed in Python 3.15, waiting for fix to propagate to <3.15.0 releases.
CVE-2026-0865
CVE-2025-15282
CVE-2026-0672
CVE-2025-15366
CVE-2025-15367
CVE-2025-11468
CVE-2025-12781
CVE-2026-1299

# Fixed in Python 3.15, waiting for fix to propagate to <3.15 releases.
CVE-2026-2297
CVE-2026-4519
CVE-2026-3298
CVE-2026-1502
CVE-2026-4224
CVE-2026-3644

# Additional CVE raised to address remaining URL corruption issue - pending fix release to <3.14.3 releases.
CVE-2026-4786

# Fix included in Python 3.14.5 release - Grype database still showing as vulnerable. Confirmed patch included in 3.14.5 (commit 48c3c7f) release, waiting for Grype DB update.
CVE-2026-6100

# base64 decode failure in Python. Fixed in Python 3.13.13 - Pending fix release to 3.12 releases. Only exploitable when parsing untrusted base64 data with `base64.b64decode()`. Use `validate=True` to mitigate in the meantime.
CVE-2026-3446

# Arbitrary file access in Python. Fixed in upstream branches with the exception of 3.12 - Pending inclusion of fix in 3.12, 3.13 and 3.14 releases. Only exploitable if uncompressing untrusted tar files with tarfile modules.
CVE-2026-11940

# Exponential archive parsing in Python. Fixed in upstream branches with the exception of 3.12 - Pending inclusion of fix in 3.12, 3.13 and 3.14 releases. Only exploitable if opening tar archives using streaming mode.
CVE-2026-11972

# Installation path traversal. Doesn't impact this image - issue only impacts the Windows installer.
CVE-2026-12003

# CRLF injection in Python. Fixed in upstream branches with the exception of 3.12 - Pending inclusion of fix in 3.12, 3.13 and 3.14 releases.
CVE-2026-0864

# HTML/Script injection in http.cookies.Morsel.js_output(). Fixed in 3.13.14, 3.14.5rc1, 3.15.0b1 - no 3.12 backport available yet.
CVE-2026-6019

# SSRF in ftplib.ftpcp() via PASV bypass. Patch committed to 3.12 branch (commit c887044) - awaiting 3.12.14 release.
CVE-2026-8328

# Path traversal via tarfile.data_filter bypass. Patch committed to 3.12 branch (commit 0d28f5e) - awaiting 3.12.14 release.
CVE-2026-7774

# CPU consumption / DoS in unicodedata.normalize(). Fixed in 3.13.14, 3.14.6, 3.15.0b2 - 3.12 backport PR open (cpython#150843), pending merge and release.
CVE-2026-3276

# Stack-based buffer overflow in bz2.BZ2Decompressor reuse after error. Fixed in 3.13.14, 3.14.6, 3.15.0b3 - 3.12 backport PR open (cpython#151057), pending merge and release.
CVE-2026-9669

# Hash flooding / insufficient entropy in xml.parsers.expat and xml.etree.ElementTree. Fixed in 3.13.14, 3.14.6, 3.15.0b2 - 3.12 backport blocked pending cpython#151401.
CVE-2026-7210

# HTML parsing / Denial of Service in html.parser. Fixed in 3.15 - awaiting fix propagation to <3.15 releases. Only exploitable when parsing untrusted HTML content with html.parser.
CVE-2026-15308

# Tar extraction / permission bypass in tarfile. Fixed in all upstream branches - awaiting release of 3.12, 3.13 and 3.14 releases. Only exploitable when extracting untrusted tar files with tarfile modules.
CVE-2026-4360

# Highest EPSS among Python 3.14 vulnerabilities (0.6%) - fixed in 3.15.0rc2. Awaiting public CVE details and formal disclosure.
CVE-2026-17084

# Tarfile vulnerability: handle a member that leaves the destination and comes back (gh-155999, PR #156000). Only exploitable when extracting untrusted tar archives. Mitigation: use tarfile.data_filter when extracting untrusted tar files.
CVE-2026-19672
CVE-2026-82049

# HTTPPasswordMgr vulnerability: credentials for https:// URI incorrectly matched against http:// URI due to scheme being discarded in reduce_uri(). Fixed in 3.15.0rc2 and backported to 3.10+ (PR #155696). Only exploitable with mixed http/https endpoints and specific urllib usage patterns.
CVE-2026-15806

# ==========================
# pip vendored dependency issues
# ==========================

# Outdated msgpack bundled inside pip's own pip/_vendor/msgpack (pip 26.2, the latest release). Not the top-level msgpack package, which is already pinned to the fixed 1.2.1 release in the Dockerfile. Only used internally by pip's HTTP cache; waiting for pip to update its vendored copy.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964

# Outdated setuptools referenced in pip's own pip/_vendor/vendor.txt (pip 26.2, the latest release). Not the top-level setuptools package, which is already pinned to the fixed 83.0.0 release in the Dockerfile. Waiting for pip to update its vendored reference.
CVE-2025-47273
CVE-2026-59890
